#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:6
msgid "Orphan Rule"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:8
msgid ""
"What prevents users from writing arbitrary trait implementations for any "
"type?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:11
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:12
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:13
msgid "// Crate `postgresql-bindings`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:16
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:28
msgid "/* details */"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:17
msgid "// Crate `database-traits`, depends on `postgresql-bindings`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:21
msgid "/* methods */"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:24
msgid "// ✅, `DbConnection` is local.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:25
msgid "// Crate `mycoolnewdb` depends on `database-traits`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:30
msgid "// ✅, `MyCoolNewDbConn` is local.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:31
msgid ""
"// Neither `PostgresqlConn` or `DbConnection` are local to `mycoolnewdb`.\n"
"// This would lead to two implementations of `DbConnection` for "
"PostgresqlConn!\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:34
msgid "// ❌🔨\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:39
msgid ""
"Rust traits should never be able to be implemented twice in its ecosystem. "
"Two implementations of the same trait for the same type is a conflict with "
"no solution."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:43
msgid ""
"We can prevent this within a crate by detecting if there are multiple "
"definitions and disallowing it, but what about between crates in the entire "
"Rust ecosystem?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:47
msgid ""
"Types are either _local_ to a crate, they are defined there, or they're not."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:49
msgid ""
"In the example's \"crates\", `PostgresqlConn` is local to `postgresql-"
"bindings`, `MyCoolNewDbConn` is local to `mycoolnewdb`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:52
msgid ""
"Traits are also either _local_ to a crate, they are defined there, or "
"they're not."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:55
msgid ""
"Again in the example, the `DbConnection` trait is local to `database-traits`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:57
msgid "If something is local, you can write trait implementations for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:59
msgid ""
"If the trait is local, you can write implementations of that trait for any "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:62
msgid ""
"If the type is local, you can write any trait implementations for that type."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:64
msgid "Outside of these boundaries, trait implementations cannot be written."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/orphan-rule.md:66
msgid ""
"This keeps implementations \"coherent\": Only one implementation of a trait "
"for a type can exist across crates."
msgstr ""

